content:
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Crossover condition 1 item 12 says AMG 510 must be held until 7 days after completion of radiation, but item 13 allows >28 days between progression scans and start of AMG 510 without specifying a maximum, potentially contradicting the 7-day hold if radiation is completed more than 21 days before start.",
      "page": 85,
      "quote": "Palliative radiation and/or surgery for new, progressive, or symptomatic lesions is permitted prior to crossover, but AMG 510 must be held until after completion of these treatments and until 7 days after completion of radiation",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Crossover condition 1 item 16 says subject has not received any other systemic anti-cancer therapies other than docetaxel during treatment phase, but item 12 permits palliative radiation and/or surgery prior to crossover, which are not systemic therapies, so no direct contradiction; however, item 15 prohibits other systemic anti-cancer agents during crossover, which is redundant but not contradictory.",
      "page": 85,
      "quote": "Subject has not received any other systemic anti-cancer therapies other than docetaxel administered during the treatment phase.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Crossover condition 2 is vague: 'Should an early efficacy of the study be noted by the DMC' lacks definition of 'early efficacy' and criteria for crossover, making it impossible to implement consistently.",
      "page": 85,
      "quote": "Should an early efficacy of the study be noted by the DMC, crossover will be considered for all subjects who randomized into the docetaxel arm (so that they will be able to immediately receive AMG 510).",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Physical measurements: weight is said to be measured 'without shoes' which is irrelevant for weight; likely a typo for 'without shoes' but weight should be without shoes? Actually weight is typically measured without shoes, but the protocol says 'Height in centimeters should be measured without shoes. Weight in kilograms should be measured without shoes.' This is a minor inconsistency: weight measurement does not require 'without shoes' specification, but it's not a contradiction.",
      "page": 86,
      "quote": "Height in centimeters should be measured without shoes.  Weight in kilograms should be measured without shoes.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Radiological imaging: screening scans must be performed within 28 days prior to cycle 1 day 1, but later says 'All subjects with brain metastasis must have MRI of the brain performed within 28 days prior to cycle 1 day 1 of AMG 510 or docetaxel.' This is consistent, but the protocol does not specify the window for subsequent brain MRI in subjects with brain metastases; it only says 'should be performed if subject has history of brain metastases' but not the frequency.",
      "page": 87,
      "quote": "All subjects with brain metastasis must have MRI of the brain performed within 28 days prior to cycle 1 day 1 of AMG 510 or docetaxel.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Independent central confirmation of progression: The protocol states that the COP will be performed by a single radiologist from a pool entirely separate from the central radiologist group reading images for efficacy, but later says 'If the evaluation of radiologic disease progression, via central imaging vendor, does not confirm progression of disease at this timepoint, a web conference may be organized... between the single radiologist and the site radiologist.' This is not contradictory but the process is unclear.",
      "page": 88,
      "quote": "The expedited independent confirmation of progression (COP) will be performed by a single radiologist from a pool of highly qualified central radiologists that is entirely separate from the central radiologist group reading the images for efficacy.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "PRO-CTCAE: The protocol says 'Subjects will complete the PRO-CTCAE questionnaire at clinic visits only (with the exception of screening visit).' This is contradictory: if they complete at clinic visits only, why exception for screening? Screening is a clinic visit, so the exception is nonsensical.",
      "page": 91,
      "quote": "Subjects will complete the PRO-CTCAE questionnaire at clinic visits only (with the exception of screening visit).",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Adverse event reporting: The protocol says AEs are reported 'after enrollment through the SFU visit' but SAEs are reported 'after signing of the informed consent through the safety follow-up visit or 30 days after the last day of dosing interval... whichever occurs later.' This is inconsistent: AEs start at enrollment, SAEs start at informed consent; enrollment is after consent, so AEs miss events between consent and enrollment.",
      "page": 92,
      "quote": "The investigator is responsible for ensuring that all adverse events observed by the investigator or reported by the subject that occur after enrollment through the SFU visit are reported using the Events CRF.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pregnancy reporting: The protocol says pregnancies are collected 'until 7 days (AMG 510) or 6 months (docetaxel) post dose for female subjects and 7 days (AMG 510) or 6 months (docetaxel) post dose for female partners of male subjects.' This is ambiguous: does 'post dose' mean after last dose? It should specify 'after last dose' but it's not a contradiction.",
      "page": 95,
      "quote": "Details of all pregnancies and/or lactation in female subjects and female partners of male subjects will be collected after the start of study treatment and until 7 days (AMG 510) or 6 months (docetaxel) post dose for female subjects and 7 days (AMG 510) or 6 months (docetaxel) post dose for female partners of male subjects.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pregnancy testing: The protocol says 'A highly sensitive (urine or serum) pregnancy test should be completed at screening and within 3 days before initiation of investigational product for females of childbearing potential.' But later says 'Females who have undergone a bilateral tubal ligation/occlusion should have pregnancy testing per protocol requirements.' This is contradictory: if they are not of childbearing potential, why require pregnancy testing?",
      "page": 96,
      "quote": "A highly sensitive (urine or serum) pregnancy test should be completed at screening and within 3 days before initiation of investigational product for females of childbearing potential.   Note:  Females who have undergone a bilateral tubal ligation/occlusion should have pregnancy testing per protocol requirements.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "PK assessments: The protocol says 'All subjects randomized to AMG 510 will have PK samples assessed.' But it does not mention PK sampling for subjects in the docetaxel arm, which is fine, but it also says 'Whole blood samples will be collected for measurement of plasma concentrations of AMG 510, metabolites' - this is fine.",
      "page": 96,
      "quote": "All subjects randomized to AMG 510 will have PK samples assessed.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Biomarker assessment: The protocol says 'A subject must have confirmation of KRAS p.G12C mutation by central laboratory testing prior to enrollment.' But later says 'Positivity for KRAS G12C will be determined at the central testing lab with an in vitro diagnostic device (Qiagen KRAS therascreen® KRAS RGQ PCR Kit).' This is consistent, but the protocol does not specify the turnaround time for central testing, which could delay enrollment.",
      "page": 96,
      "quote": "A subject must have confirmation of KRAS p.G12C mutation by central laboratory testing prior to enrollment.",
      "severity": "minor"
    }
  ]
}
